course: dictionary
lesson: 12698
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. «Doctored» is one of them. The words around it are its context, and they tell you which meaning to use. «The photo had been doctored to make the fish look bigger.» The clues are photo and make the fish look bigger, so doctored means changed in a dishonest way.
explain: «The nurse doctored Sam's grazed elbow and put a plaster on it.» Now the clues are nurse, grazed elbow and plaster. Doctored means treated in a simple way, as a nurse or doctor would. Try the meaning in the sentence: does treated fit? Yes, so you have found the right one.
explain: The third meaning is about pets. «The vet doctored the farm dog so it could not have puppies.» This meaning is old-fashioned and mostly used in America. Today most people say neutered. When a word has several meanings, test each one in the sentence and keep the one that fits best.
fact: Doctored is a verb and an adjective. Its forms are doctor, doctors, doctored and doctoring.
fact: «Doctored» can mean changed in a dishonest way, as in «a doctored photo».
fact: «Doctored» can mean treated in a simple way, for example a cut or a scrape.
fact: For a pet, «doctored» means neutered: had an operation so it cannot have babies. This sense is old-fashioned and mostly American.
fact: The dishonest meaning is very common in news reports and police talk, so you will meet it often.
exercise: «The photo had been doctored, so the fish looked twice as big as it really was.» What does doctored mean here? | Cooked in a hot oven | Taken on a sunny day | Measured with a ruler | *Changed in a dishonest way
exercise: «The nurse doctored Sam's grazed elbow and gave him a plaster.» What does doctored mean here? | *Treated in a simple way | Broken into pieces | Hidden under a blanket | Painted in bright colours
exercise: «The farm dog was doctored so it could not have puppies.» Which meaning fits? | Given a new name | Lost in a park | Trained to fetch sticks | *Neutered, so it cannot have puppies
test: «The news report said the video had been doctored by someone who wanted to fool people.» What does doctored mean? | *Changed in a dishonest way | Made louder with music | Watched by millions | Filmed on a phone
test: «The vet doctored the old cat last week, so it will not have kittens.» What does doctored mean here? | Taken for a walk | Given a new collar | *Neutered, so it cannot have kittens | Fed with extra fish
exam: When you meet «doctored» in a text, what should you do first? | *Read the words around it and test each meaning in the sentence | Skip it and never read the sentence again | Guess from the number of letters in the word | Look only at the first letter
